WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.335 --> 00:00:17.397
Just a few days before Jo was to leave, she received a letter from Beth telling her about Meg's pregnancy.

2
00:00:17.398 --> 00:00:23.752
Coincidentally it was the Professor who delivered the mail to Jo that day, so she shared the good news with him.

3
00:00:23.753 --> 00:00:27.805
"I can't believe I'm going to be an aunt!" she shouted in delight.

4
00:00:27.806 --> 00:00:32.474
For some reason, the idea of Meg getting married had been hard for Jo to accept,

5
00:00:32.475 --> 00:00:37.828
but news that she was going to have a little niece or nephew completely thrilled her.

6
00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:41.584
"You like children, don't you?" the Professor asked.

7
00:00:41.585 --> 00:00:48.336
Nodding enthusiastically Jo said, "I love their innocence, their curiosity, their energy, and their humor.

8
00:00:48.337 --> 00:00:52.935
That's why if I don't succeed as an author, I am going to become a teacher."

9
00:00:52.936 --> 00:00:58.015
Jo remembered the strange look that the Professor had given her when she made that comment.

10
00:00:58.016 --> 00:01:09.233
He said, "Then perhaps our paths may cross again one day, Jo, because it is my dream to start a school for boys, and I could use a good teacher like you."

11
00:01:09.234 --> 00:01:15.104
Suddenly feeling shy, Jo merely said, "I didn't realize you had such plans.

12
00:01:15.105 --> 00:01:18.975
One day, I hope you see your dream come true."

13
00:01:18.976 --> 00:01:26.578
Now, as Jo sat packing her bags, she wondered what her dreams were and how they had changed in these past few months.

14
00:01:26.579 --> 00:01:29.795
A light knock on the door broke into her thoughts.

15
00:01:29.796 --> 00:01:36.684
"Come in if you can find room for your feet," Jo called out, trying to clear some space among all her belongings scattered everywhere.

16
00:01:36.685 --> 00:01:42.118
"I thought you only had a few things," the Professor joked as he looked around the messy room.

17
00:01:42.119 --> 00:01:47.463
"I guess I must have acquired one or two more things while I was here," Jo said, chuckling.

18
00:01:47.464 --> 00:01:51.426
"Will your bag be able to hold one more small item?" he asked.

19
00:01:51.427 --> 00:01:55.268
"I'm sure I can find some space somewhere," Jo replied.

20
00:01:55.269 --> 00:01:59.590
"I want to give you this," the Professor said, holding out a wrapped parcel.

21
00:01:59.591 --> 00:02:07.667
Inside was a leather notebook with her initials on the cover. "Oh, it's beautiful!" exclaimed Jo.

22
00:02:07.668 --> 00:02:11.898
"For you to record your dreams," the Professor said smiling.

23
00:02:11.899 --> 00:02:16.502
Swallowing the lump in her throat, Jo placed the notebook inside her handbag.

24
00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:23.885
"Also, I want to thank you for this," the Professor said as he took his shoes off and proudly wiggled his mended socks.

25
00:02:23.886 --> 00:02:27.693
"How did you know?" laughed Jo.

26
00:02:27.694 --> 00:02:32.651
"When I saw the girls sewing, I knew these stitches belonged to you," he said.

27
00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:38.678
An awkward silence followed. Then the Professor finally said, "Will you be returning to New York?"

28
00:02:38.679 --> 00:02:44.056
"I would like to, but I can't say with certainty," Jo said honestly.

29
00:02:44.057 --> 00:02:50.004
"I hope we will meet again, Jo March," the Professor said with feeling as he held out his hand.

30
00:02:50.005 --> 00:02:55.897
Smiling as she took his hand, Jo said, "It's been a pleasure knowing you, Fritz."

31
00:02:55.898 --> 00:03:02.490
As Jo finished packing her belongings, Amy was almost done with gathering everything into her luggage.

32
00:03:02.491 --> 00:03:07.856
The following day, she and Aunt March were heading toward their next destination: Italy.

33
00:03:07.857 --> 00:03:13.707
Amy could hardly sleep that night because she had dreamt about visiting Italy since she was a little girl.

34
00:03:13.708 --> 00:03:20.898
"I guess some things do remain the same," she thought, thinking of her longstanding dream to see that beautiful country.

35
00:03:20.899 --> 00:03:25.750
But Amy had changed in many other ways as she was learning on this trip to Europe.

36
00:03:25.751 --> 00:03:30.012
Reflecting on the relationship between Aunt March and Amy's own family,

37
00:03:30.013 --> 00:03:35.372
Amy appreciated the worth of close family ties and the values her parents had taught her.

38
00:03:35.373 --> 00:03:39.970
She concluded that it was love, not money, that bonded people closely.

39
00:03:39.971 --> 00:03:46.302
That was why she could not marry Fred: she didn't love him, much to the disappointment of Aunt March.

40
00:03:46.303 --> 00:03:53.303
"I have a feeling that something wonderful is waiting for me in Italy," Amy said to herself as she lay in bed.

41
00:03:53.304 --> 00:03:59.145
Jo's homecoming was so heartwarming that she forgot about her friends in New York for a moment.

42
00:03:59.146 --> 00:04:03.043
"You look different somehow, darling," her mother commented.

43
00:04:03.044 --> 00:04:07.504
"Like a lady," teased her father, playfully touching her stylish bun.

44
00:04:07.505 --> 00:04:12.695
"Mrs. Kirke taught me how to do my hair up in different ways," Jo said proudly.

45
00:04:12.696 --> 00:04:18.711
"I'm so glad you're home," Beth said quietly. "It's as if you never left."

46
00:04:18.712 --> 00:04:23.611
In Jo's eyes though, much had changed during her absence, most notably Beth.

47
00:04:23.612 --> 00:04:30.405
She looked thinner, paler, and lifeless; a total contrast from the sunny, happy girl in Jo's memory.

48
00:04:30.406 --> 00:04:38.715
When Jo told her Mother her worries, Mother shook her head and just said, "She's never really been the same since the fever."

49
00:04:38.716 --> 00:04:46.509
Early the next morning, Jo decided to brave the cold and took her new leather notebook and extra sweater to the pond behind their house.

50
00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:54.414
She was looking forward to having a private moment to reflect upon her trip, but when she got to the lake, someone was already there.

51
00:04:54.415 --> 00:05:00.170
"Laurie!" she called out excitedly, truly happy to see her best friend.

52
00:05:00.171 --> 00:05:04.160
"Jo! What are you doing here?" he asked, alarmed.

53
00:05:04.161 --> 00:05:07.392
"I'm back, you know," she laughed.

54
00:05:07.393 --> 00:05:12.589
"I know," he smiled. "I was going to come see you later on in the morning."

55
00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:16.459
"I never knew you came down here to the pond," she said.

56
00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:21.814
"I walk down here most mornings," he said, adding, "You don't know everything about me."

57
00:05:21.815 --> 00:05:31.199
"Well, I'm so glad to see you and I have so much to tell you," Jo said, trying to change the subject because she felt uneasy tension between them.

58
00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:36.291
"So do I, Jo," Laurie said quietly as he stared at her for a long time.

59
00:05:36.292 --> 00:05:42.150
"Laurie, " Jo began, thinking she knew what he was about to say but not wanting him to say it,

60
00:05:42.151 --> 00:05:45.886
because once it came out, their friendship would never be the same.

61
00:05:45.887 --> 00:05:51.490
Laurie abruptly interrupted her. "This may not be the best time to say this but I don't care.

62
00:05:51.491 --> 00:05:55.009
After you left, my life has been nothing but agony.

63
00:05:55.010 --> 00:06:02.199
I went back to college, and by the way, you'll be happy to know that I received the highest marks in my class and will graduate with honors."

64
00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:05.760
"That's wonderful, Laurie! I knew you could do it! I'm so . . ."

65
00:06:05.761 --> 00:06:13.845
Congratulating him, Jo prayed she would be able to say a few words before Laurie went on, but he continued as if he didn't hear her.

66
00:06:13.846 --> 00:06:22.682
"From the first day I met you all those years ago until this very moment, my feelings for you have never changed and they never will," he said passionately.

67
00:06:22.683 --> 00:06:30.699
Taking her hand, Laurie said, "Jo, my life, no matter how good it is, will never be complete unless you are in it."

68
00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:38.515
Feeling as though her heart was being broken, Jo somehow found the strength to say what she could no longer hold back.

69
00:06:38.516 --> 00:06:41.836
"Laurie, please don't do this," she begged him.

70
00:06:41.837 --> 00:06:47.037
"Our friendship is the most precious thing to me, and I don't want it to change.

71
00:06:47.038 --> 00:06:50.466
I can't be the kind of person you want me to be."

72
00:06:50.467 --> 00:06:54.938
Laurie bowed his head, his face crushed with pain.

73
00:06:54.939 --> 00:06:57.214
"I don't love you like that, Laurie.

74
00:06:57.215 --> 00:07:05.585
I never have," said Jo to her dearest friend in the most brutal yet truthful words.
